{"url": "https://doi.org/10.1002/fut.21715", "title": "The Impact of Sampling Frequency on Intraday Correlation and Lead–Lag Relationships Between Index Futures and Individual Stocks", "engine": "exa", "published": "2015-03-16", "snippet": "Transaction costs, liquidity effects, capital limits, and regulatory restrictions reduce arbitrage efficiency and weaken the link between futures prices and their underlying stocks. This study examines how the sampling frequency for return calculation affects the intraday correlation and the lead–lag relationship between the Hong Kong Hang Seng Index futures, the underlying cash index, an exchange‐traded fund (ETF) that mimics the index, and each component stock. The paper uses firm bid and offer quotes to eliminate the negative bias in measuring the correlation between the futures and the less liquid stocks. The sampling frequency significantly affects the futures‐stock dynamic relationship, particularly for small‐cap stocks. The overall results indicate that market participants trade ETF and the largest index's constituent stocks to capitalize on index arbitrage opportunities. The lag of the cash index is greatest against futures price movement, a reflection of the adverse impact of stale prices on the informational role of stock indexes. © 2015 Wiley Periodicals, Inc. Jrl Fut Mark 35:939–952, 2015\n...\n- Ben R. Marshall, Nhut H. Nguyen, Nuttawat Visaltanachoti. ETF arbitrage: Intraday evidence. Journal of Banking & Finance. 2013;37(9):3486-3498. doi:10.1016/j.jbankfin.2013.05.014.\n\n---", "extra": {}, "read_via": "exa_fetch", "text_chars": 4919, "excerpt": "# The Impact of Sampling Frequency on Intraday Correlation and Lead–Lag Relationships Between Index Futures and Individual Stocks URL: https://doi.org/10.1002/fut.21715 Published: 2015-03-16 Author: Joseph K. W. Fung, Francis Lau, Yiuman Tse # The Impact of Sampling Frequency on Intraday Correlation and Lead–Lag Relationships Between Index Futures and Individual Stocks Journal of Futures Markets. ", "jev": {"concrete": 0.05, "evidence": "none", "evidence_confidence": 0.88, "market": "derivatives", "us_long_only": 0.38, "recent": 0.01, "code": 0.04}, "priority": 0.003}
